A narrow reconstruction of the due-diligence ladder is $\text{deck}
\longrightarrow
\text{conversation}
\longrightarrow
\text{context}
\longrightarrow
\text{character}
\longrightarrow
\text{alignment}.$ The last word is the strongest. On boards, and among people brought in to help companies, Williams wants shared respect and a shared goal. The objective is to make the play successful, not to be the brightest light in the room.

